 "parts": [
  "Why does a pen cap have a tiny hole?",
  "It is not a mistake.",
  "You might guess it is for the ink.",
  "According to its maker, it is there for safety.",
  "Children put things in their mouths. And a pen cap is small enough to fit.",
  "A cap that gets inhaled can block the airway.",
  "A twenty twenty-four case report described three children who inhaled pen caps.",
  "Since nineteen ninety-one, the classic Bic Cristal cap has had a tiny hole.",
  "The point is to reduce the risk of suffocation if the cap is inhaled.",
  "Our reading: it is a tiny air path.",
  "If the cap gets stuck, some air may still pass.",
  "There is even an international standard on pen caps and asphyxiation. I S O eleven five forty.",
  "We read only its title and scope.",
  "The hole reduces the risk. It is not a promise.",
  "Keep small caps away from little kids."
 ],
